    "two-hundred-years-together": {
      "title": "Two Hundred Years Together",
      "description": "Untitled children’s book (in progress).",
      "banner": {
        "src": "hyenas.jpg",
        "alt": "Two Hundred Years Together"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p>“Two Hundred Years Together,” written by Matthew Hasson and illustrated by Shannon Collins. <br><br>This project was a collaboration with a friend who wanted to propose to his girlfriend by presenting a poem he had written in children’s book form. I ended up taking longer than expected to finish the illustrations while juggling parenthood and a heavy workload, so the book ended up being a wedding gift for his fiancée. </p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "gallery",
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "tortoise-shell-greens.jpg",
              "alt": "tortoise shell-greens.jpg"
            },
            {
              "src": "tortoises.jpg",
              "alt": " I wish we were giant tortoises,  So the days would go by slow. For two hundred years we’d be together, I know it to be so. "
            },
            {
              "src": "birds.jpg",
              "alt": " And if we were two birds, Like a cardinal, hawk, or jay, If you ever got lonely, I’d fly to you right away. "
            },
            {
              "src": "whales.jpg",
              "alt": " If we were humpback whales, swimming leagues across the sea, To always have you by my side, What an adventure that would be! "
            },
            {
              "src": "monkeys.jpg",
              "alt": " If we were arctic monkeys, In a frigid, icy, storm, We’d nestle our bodies close, To keep each other warm. "
            },
            {
              "src": "bees.jpg",
              "alt": " If we were honey bees, Buzzing about the morning dew, No queen could ever take your place, No nectar sweeter than you. "
            },
            {
              "src": "hyenas-6388cf.jpg",
              "alt": " If we were hyenas, Rolling ‘round the dirt, We’d always make each other laugh, Sometimes so much it hurts. "
            },
            {
              "src": "skunks-1.jpg",
              "alt": " If we were skunks, You wouldn’t need a shower, Cause even if you stunk too much, To me you’d smell like flowers. "
            },
            {
              "src": "trees.jpg",
              "alt": " If we were a couple trees, Standing tall and apart, Below the surface we’d share a root, Which keeps us close at heart. "
            },
            {
              "src": "clouds-1.jpg",
              "alt": " If we were two clouds, Making shapes in swirls of white, From way up in the sky, You’d still be the best view in sight. "
            },
            {
              "src": "rocksjpg.jpg",
              "alt": " If we were two rocks, Just laying on the ground, I’d never be bored, As long as you’re around. "
            },
            {
              "src": "watercolor-vivid-1.jpg",
              "alt": " If we were anything other than us,  We’d still be best friends… "
            },
            {
              "src": "dogs-1.jpg",
              "alt": " Two hundred years we’d be together, I know it to be true, Because no matter where we go in life, You got me and I got you. "
            },
            {
              "src": "tortoise-shell-purples.jpg",
              "alt": "tortoise-shell-purples.jpg"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
